{
  "public_post": "Update: All bread sold by the co‑op today is being recalled; refunds will be available at the bakery. We are securing a safe flour supply and will resume baking tomorrow. Please do NOT eat any co‑op bread until further notice.",
  "coop_message": "Team, we need to: (1) set up a refund station at the bakery for today's loaves, (2) contact the village health official to report the contamination and get guidance, (3) order a verified safe flour batch ASAP, (4) schedule a clean‑up and sanitisation of the bakery tonight, and (5) plan to resume baking tomorrow with the new flour. Let's meet at 5 PM to assign tasks.",
  "reason": "We must inform residents of the recall and coordinate immediate remediation steps within the co‑op."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important: All bread sold by the co‑op this week is unsafe. Please do not eat any co‑op bread and bring any loaves you bought to the bakery for a full refund; we are securing safe flour and will resume safe sales tomorrow.",
  "coop_message": "Confirm contamination; initiate recall of all loaves sold this week and issue refunds, contact the village health officer, order a certified safe flour batch, and schedule an emergency bake for tomorrow—meeting at 10 am at the bakery.",
  "reason": "We must protect villagers' health, manage the recall, and restore trust before resuming sales."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important: All co‑op bread is currently unsafe due to contaminated flour; we have halted sales and are recalling any bread sold. Please obtain bread from the farm stand until further notice.",
  "coop_message": "All members: Immediate actions – 1) Recall any loaves sold yesterday and issue refunds; 2) Notify the village health official of the contamination; 3) Secure and discard the contaminated flour batch; 4) Source safe replacement flour (contact supplier/farm); 5) Arrange temporary bread supply via the farm stand; meet at the bakery at 10 am to coordinate.",
  "reason": "To protect villagers' health, comply with safety protocols, and coordinate the co‑op's response."
}

{
  "public_post": "Update: All bread sold yesterday is being recalled; please return any loaves you purchased for a full refund, and do NOT eat any co‑op bread until we confirm it is safe. We are sourcing safe flour and will resume tomorrow.",
  "coop_message": "Health official has been notified; start recall process today, set up a refund desk at the bakery, secure a safe flour batch from supplier X, and meet at 3 PM to plan tomorrow's production.",
  "reason": "We need to manage the recall, refunds, and safe resumption while keeping villagers informed."
}

{
  "public_post": "Update: Refunds for all co‑op bread sold this week are available at the bakery; we have secured a certified safe flour batch and will resume baking tomorrow. If you feel ill after eating our bread, please see the clinic. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "Refund desk is operational; confirm delivery of the certified safe flour batch by 8 am tomorrow; assign bakers for an emergency bake at 9 am; ensure tonight's sanitation is complete and schedule health‑official inspection before reopening.",
  "reason": "Residents need clear info on refunds and resumption, while the co‑op must finalize logistics for safe production."
}

{
  "public_post": "Update: Safe flour has arrived and the bakery is fully sanitized. We will resume selling co‑op bread starting today. The refund desk remains open for any loaves purchased on days 1‑2—please collect refunds or exchange them for fresh bread. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "Safe flour batch X delivered; bakery cleaned overnight. Assign baking team to start production at 8 am, keep the refund desk open until all contaminated loaves are returned, and notify the health official of the safe resumption and request clearance; continue monitoring for any illness reports.",
  "reason": "Residents need to know baking has safely resumed and refunds are still available, while co‑op members coordinate the final recall and production steps."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: Fresh, safe co‑op bread is back on sale today (day 4) with a 10 % discount as a thank‑you for your patience—refunds for any contaminated loaves remain available at the bakery.",
  "coop_message": "Team, please keep the refund desk open through the day, monitor any illness reports, and ensure the new batch is labeled ‘Day 4 – Safe Flour’; also, let’s note sales numbers for the village report.",
  "reason": "To announce safe resumption of sales and maintain transparency while encouraging purchases."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news, villagers: the bakery has been fully sanitized, we are using certified safe flour, and the village health officer has cleared us to resume selling fresh bread today. Refunds for any contaminated loaves are still available at the bakery. Thank you for your patience and trust.",
  "coop_message": "Health officer clearance received; open the bakery for sales at 8 am, keep the refund desk open until all returns are processed, and assign bakers (Jade, Fay) to the emergency bake. Monitor any illness reports and update the health officer if needed.",
  "reason": "To announce safe resumption of bread sales and coordinate final reopening steps with the co‑op."
}

{
  "public_post": "Update: The village clinic has reported two cases of stomach illness today. We are working closely with the health officer to investigate and ensure our bread is safe. Please do NOT eat any co‑op bread purchased today until we give the all‑clear. Refunds for any loaves bought today are available at the bakery.",
  "coop_message": "Team, the health officer has flagged two illness reports linked to today's sales. Halt all bread sales immediately, set up an extra refund desk, and send a sample of today's batch for testing. Notify the clinic of our recall and consider sourcing temporary bread from the farm stand while we verify safety.",
  "reason": "We must protect residents' health and maintain trust after new illness reports."
}

{
  "public_post": "Update: Our bakery continues to use certified safe flour and has health officer clearance. If you purchased bread on days 1‑2 and have not yet returned it, refunds are still available today. The recent stomach illnesses reported are being investigated; please contact the clinic if you feel unwell. Fresh bread remains safe to eat.",
  "coop_message": "Health officer confirmed safety of the current batch; keep the refund desk open for any remaining contaminated loaves; monitor sales and illness reports closely; if any new cases arise, suspend sales immediately and conduct rapid testing.",
  "reason": "To reassure villagers about the safety of current bread while ensuring we handle remaining refunds and stay ready to act on any new health issues."
}

{
  "public_post": "Urgent notice: The flour batch used for all co‑op bread this week was contaminated and has caused illness. We are recalling every loaf sold this week. Please return any bread to the bakery for a full refund. We sincerely apologize and will work with the health officer to ensure safety and provide compensation.",
  "coop_message": "Team, we must immediately halt all sales, set up a full recall desk, issue refunds for every loaf sold this week, notify the health officer and village council, and discuss compensation and legal steps; meet today at 9 am to coordinate the response.",
  "reason": "The lab confirmed contamination, so we must be transparent and initiate a full recall."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important: We are temporarily suspending co‑op bread sales today (day 6) while we complete final safety testing after recent illness reports. All loaves purchased on any day can be returned for a full refund or exchanged for safe bread once cleared. We apologize for the inconvenience and will update you as soon as we have results.",
  "coop_message": "Team, the health officer has flagged illness reports linked to today's batch; we must halt sales immediately, set up an extra refund desk, send today's batch for testing, and keep the clinic informed. Keep the refund desk open for all previous loaves, continue monitoring any new cases, and prepare a clear communication plan for villagers once we have results.",
  "reason": "To protect residents after recent stomach illness reports and coordinate an immediate safety response."
}

{
  "public_post": "Urgent: All co‑op bread sold this week is contaminated and unsafe. Effective immediately, stop buying any co‑op bread. Return any loaves to the bakery today for a full refund or exchange. We will use the farm stand for bread until we can guarantee safety. We apologize for the danger and inconvenience.",
  "coop_message": "Lab results confirm the entire flour batch used this week is contaminated. We must halt all sales immediately, discard all remaining inventory, keep the refund desk open, notify the health officer and clinic, arrange a full recall, and secure a verified safe flour supply. Meeting at 9 am today to coordinate these actions.",
  "reason": "The lab result shows the whole week's flour is unsafe and recent illness reports confirm the risk."
}
